<title>FRANCE: ALPINE SKIING-MEN'S WORLD CUP SUPER-G WINNER PROFILE.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-MEN'S WORLD CUP SUPER-G WINNER PROFILE.</headline>
<dateline>VAL D'ISERE, France 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Profile of the</p>
<p>winner of Monday's men's World Cup super-G race:</p>
<p>Name: Hans Knauss</p>
<p>Age: 25</p>
<p>Nation: Austria</p>
<p>Previous World Cup victories: one giant slalom in Alta Badia</p>
<p>in 1996, one super-G in Valloire in 1995.</p>
<p>Other facts: finished second in the super-G World Cup</p>
<p>standings last season. Had a nose operation last spring to solve</p>
<p>breathing problems.</p>
</text>
